Id: pam002w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_pam
References: pwquality.conf(5), NIST SP 800-63B
Controls: CIS 5.2; NIST IA-5(1); ISO 5.17, 8.5; CE User access control

Passwords are checked for quality, but the minimum length allowed is
below 8 characters (minlen= on the pam_pwquality or pam_cracklib line,
or in /etc/security/pwquality.conf). Length matters more than any
other rule: each character multiplies the guesses needed.

To fix it, set minlen = 14 in /etc/security/pwquality.conf (CIS); NIST
SP 800-63B asks for at least 8. A minlen= on the module's line in
/etc/pam.d overrides the file.
